<h1>Handler Layer: HTTP Request Processing</h1>

<div class="hero">
<div class="subtitle">HTTP API Entry Points</div>
<p>The handler package translates HTTP requests into domain objects, validates inputs, enforces authorization, and formats responses. Each handler delegates business logic to services.</p>
</div>

<main id="main">

<div class="intro-box">
<h3>Overview</h3>
<p>Handlers are the <strong>outermost API boundary</strong>. They receive HTTP requests from Gin, parse and validate them, call services, and send back JSON responses. This separation keeps business logic testable and transport-agnostic.</p>
<p><strong>Key principle:</strong> Handlers should be thin. If a handler exceeds ~50 lines, logic belongs in a service.</p>
</div>

<h2>Request Processing Flow</h2>
<div class="diagram-container">
<pre><code>HTTP Request
    |
    v
Gin Router (matches path)
    |
    v
Middleware (auth, CORS, logging)
    |
    v
Handler.Validate() (check JWT, unmarshal JSON)
    |
    v
Handler.Call Service (business logic)
    |
    v
Service returns (data, error)
    |
    v
Handler.Marshal Response (JSON)
    |
    v
Gin sends HTTP 200/4xx/5xx
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2>Handler Types</h2>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Handler</th><th>Endpoints</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>ChatHandler</strong></td><td>POST /chat, GET /chat/:id</td><td>Conversational AI. Streams responses, manages context window.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>SearchHandler</strong></td><td>POST /search, GET /search/stats</td><td>Full-text + semantic search. Returns ranked results with snippets.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>KBHandler</strong></td><td>POST /kb, DELETE /kb/:id</td><td>Knowledge base CRUD. Manages documents, indexes.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>DocumentHandler</strong></td><td>PUT /doc/:id, GET /doc/:id/chunks</td><td>Document operations. Upload, delete, reprocess.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FileHandler</strong></td><td>POST /file/upload, GET /file/:id</td><td>File I/O wrapper. Delegates to storage backend.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>LLMHandler</strong></td><td>POST /llm/chat, POST /llm/embed</td><td>LLM API proxy. Routes to provider (OpenAI, local).</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>ChunkHandler</strong></td><td>GET /chunk/:id, PATCH /chunk/:id</td><td>Text chunk operations. Inspect, edit, rerank.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>Handler Anatomy</h2>

<h3>Input Validation</h3>
<p>Every handler validates HTTP inputs before calling services:</p>
<pre><code>type ChatRequest struct {
    KnowledgeBaseID string `json:"kb_id" binding:"required"`
    Question        string `json:"question" binding:"required,max=2000"`
    MaxTokens       int    `json:"max_tokens" binding:"gte=10,lte=4000"`
}

func (h *ChatHandler) Chat(c *gin.Context) {
    var req ChatRequest
    if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&req); err != nil {
        c.JSON(400, gin.H{"error": err.Error()})
        return
    }
    // Input is now type-safe and validated
}</code></pre>

<h3>Authorization</h3>
<p>Middleware extracts JWT and injects user/tenant context. Handlers check scopes:</p>
<pre><code>func (h *ChatHandler) Chat(c *gin.Context) {
    userID := c.GetString("user_id")     // from JWT
    tenantID := c.GetString("tenant_id")
    
    if userID == "" {
        c.JSON(401, gin.H{"error": "unauthorized"})
        return
    }
    
    // Ensure user owns the KB
    kb, err := h.service.GetKB(c.Context(), tenantID, kbID)
    if err != nil || kb.OwnerID != userID {
        c.JSON(403, gin.H{"error": "forbidden"})
        return
    }
}</code></pre>

<h3>Service Invocation</h3>
<p>Delegate to service; let it handle retries, caching, transactions:</p>
<pre><code>result, err := h.chatService.Chat(c.Context(), &ChatRequest{
    KnowledgeBaseID: req.KnowledgeBaseID,
    Question:        req.Question,
    UserID:          userID,
    TenantID:        tenantID,
})
if err != nil {
    h.logger.Error("chat error", "user_id", userID, "error", err)
    c.JSON(500, gin.H{"error": "internal error"})
    return
}</code></pre>

<h3>Response Formatting</h3>
<p>Return consistent, typed responses:</p>
<pre><code>type ChatResponse struct {
    ID        string    `json:"id"`
    Answer    string    `json:"answer"`
    Tokens    int       `json:"tokens"`
    Sources   []Source  `json:"sources"`
    Latency   float64   `json:"latency_ms"`
}

c.JSON(200, gin.H{
    "data": result,
    "meta": gin.H{
        "request_id": c.GetString("request_id"),
        "timestamp": time.Now().Unix(),
    },
})</code></pre>

<h2>Error Handling</h2>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>When</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>400</strong></td><td>Invalid input (missing field, wrong type)</td><td>missing kb_id parameter</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>401</strong></td><td>Missing or invalid JWT</td><td>expired token</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>403</strong></td><td>User lacks permission</td><td>accessing other tenant's KB</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>404</strong></td><td>Resource not found</td><td>KB not in database</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>429</strong></td><td>Rate limit exceeded</td><td>user quota hit</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>500</strong></td><td>Unexpected service error</td><td>database connection lost</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

